&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Software Engineer, you will play a critical role in developing and implementing secure software solutions to protect our systems and data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job description:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This section contains the key objectives for the role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, execution, deployment, monitoring and maintaining software engineering applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active participation in Code Reviews and production deployments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take project requirements and map them to technical design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively participate in architecture design teams as a key contributor to product definition and future implementation planning&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Work closely with frontend and other backend development teams to ensure the platform is built to support their needs&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with service engineering (SRE) teams to ensure platform is built with scalability &amp;amp; ease of deployment and maintenance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build reusable APIs for internal and external use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Documentation of standard practices adopted in the platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team building activities and helping with recruitment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5 years of experience in IT Industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Domain experience within Invest areas (i.e. Stocks, Crypto and Funds) for bank or Fintech.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands on experience/knowledge with TDD, OOP, FP and software design patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with Amazon Web Services / Cloud&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good exposure in CI/CD adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4 yrs strong NODE tech stack- MUST&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong back end with AI knowledge and/or experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
