&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary: &lt;/strong&gt;The IAM Operations &amp;amp; Access Review Support Analyst is responsible for executing day-to-day IAM operational activities, supporting access reviews, identity lifecycle management, privileged access administration, and access governance processes. The role ensures timely provisioning, deprovisioning, reconciliation, and certification activities across the organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Identity Lifecycle Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute Joiner, Mover, Leaver (JML) processes in accordance with approved procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provision, modify, and revoke user access across enterprise applications and platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure timely onboarding and offboarding of employees, contractors, and third parties.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privileged Access Management (PAM)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer privileged accounts and access requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform credential reconciliations and privileged account reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support privileged access certifications and monitoring activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate and remediate orphaned or dormant privileged accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Access Reviews &amp;amp; Recertification&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support execution of periodic user access reviews and certification campaigns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with application owners and business managers on access attestations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow up on overdue certifications and remediation actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate certification reports and evidence for compliance purposes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Monitoring &amp;amp; Reporting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor provisioning SLA performance and operational metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support exception management and issue escalation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate operational records and audit trails.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Audit &amp;amp; Compliance Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide operational evidence for audits and compliance assessments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support closure of audit findings through remediation actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain documentation and records of access management activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–5 years of experience in IAM Operations, Access Administration, Service Management, or Security Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Identity Governance &amp;amp; Administration (IGA) and PAM solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of JML processes, Active Directory, LDAP, and access certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and process discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SailPoint, Saviynt, Entra ID, CyberArk, BeyondTrust, Okta, or similar IAM platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ITIL Foundation, Security+, or equivalent certifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

